ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the comparative correlative construction \('The more... the more'\) in expressing biophysical proportional relationships.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Syntactic Architecture of Comparative Correlatives:) Tj
T*
(   The comparative correlative construction \(also known as the 'double comparative'\) pairs two) Tj
T*
(   parallel clauses, each introduced by the definite article 'the' governing a comparative) Tj
T*
(   adjective or adverb:) Tj
T*
(   - Formula: The + [Comparative Expression] + [Subject 1 + Verb 1], the + [Comparative) Tj
T*
(   Expression] + [Subject 2 + Verb 2].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Role in Articulating Kinetic and Physical Proportionalities:) Tj
T*
(   - Direct Proportionality:) Tj
T*
(   - "The higher the incubation temperature, the faster the enzymatic reaction proceeds.") Tj
T*
(   - "The greater the molecular weight of the solute, the slower its diffusion across the matrix.") Tj
T*
(   - Inverse Proportionality:) Tj
T*
(   - "The lower the dissociation constant \(Kd\), the higher the antibody binding affinity.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Punctuation and Ellipsis:) Tj
T*
(   - The two clauses must be separated by a comma.) Tj
T*
(   - When the verbs are copular \('is/are'\), they are frequently ellipted in concise mathematical) Tj
T*
(   discourse:) Tj
T*
(   - "The smaller the pore size, the greater the trans-membrane resistance.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine distributive determiners: 'Each', 'Every', 'Either', and 'Neither' in experimental replicates and factorial designs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Distributive Syntax Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   Distributive determiners consider members of a group individually rather than collectively.) Tj
T*
(   They consistently take singular countable nouns and mandate singular verbs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Functional Contrast:) Tj
T*
(   - Each: Focuses on individual constituent items considered one by one. Applicable to sets of) Tj
T*
(   two or more:) Tj
T*
(   - "Each reaction well was loaded with 50 uL of master mix.") Tj
T*
(   - "Each of the two duplicate tubes showed high luminescence.") Tj
T*
(   - Every: Considers all members of a group together without exception, yet remains grammatically) Tj
T*
(   singular. Applicable strictly to sets of three or more:) Tj
T*
(   - "Every participant in the trial signed an informed consent form.") Tj
T*
(   - Either: Refers to one or the other of exactly two entities:) Tj
T*
(   - "Either candidate buffer is suitable for gel electrophoresis.") Tj
T*
(   - Neither: Negative disjunctive referring to not one and not the other of two entities:) Tj
T*
(   - "Neither recombinant strain demonstrated antibiotic resistance.") Tj
T*
ET

