/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine article usage before numerical expressions, percentages, fractions, and laboratory orders of magnitude.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Numerical Determiner Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   - Fractions: Expressed with an indefinite article before the fractional denominator:) Tj
T*
(   - "a third of the volume", "a quarter of an hour", "half an hour" \(or "a half hour"\).) Tj
T*
(   - Percentages: Percentages take zero article or definite article depending on syntactic) Tj
T*
(   function:) Tj
T*
(   - "Ten percent of the cells were viable." \(Zero article\).) Tj
T*
(   - "The ten percent who completed the study showed improvement." \(Definite article\).) Tj
T*
(   - Orders of Magnitude:) Tj
T*
(   - "The viral titer increased by an order of magnitude." \(Takes 'an'\).) Tj
T*
(   - "by a factor of ten." \(Takes 'a'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Specific Units of Measure:) Tj
T*
(   - "5 milligrams a day", "60 drops a minute", "100 dollars an assay". \(Indefinite article) Tj
T*
(   expressing rate\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 21:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the subtle error of repeating versus omitting the definite article before coordinate nouns.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Coreferential Single Entity Rule:) Tj
T*
(   When two nouns joined by 'and' refer to the SAME single person, office, or unified physical) Tj
T*
(   object, only ONE article is used at the beginning:) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "The inventor and founder of the biotechnology startup was awarded the Nobel Prize.") Tj
T*
(   - Analysis: One article \('The'\) signals that the inventor and founder are one and the same) Tj
T*
(   human individual. The verb is singular \('was'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Distinct Separate Entities Rule:) Tj
T*
(   When two nouns joined by 'and' refer to TWO DISTINCT separate individuals or entities, the) Tj
T*
(   article MUST be repeated before the second noun:) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "The inventor and the founder of the biotechnology startup were awarded the Nobel) Tj
T*
(   Prize.") Tj
T*
(   - Analysis: Two articles \('The... and the...'\) prove that two distinct individuals are being) Tj
T*
ET

