(>> Solution to Question 25:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the definite article 'the' with academic degrees, certifications, and professional honors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Degree Titles:) Tj
T*
(   - Generic Mention \(Takes Indefinite Article\):) Tj
T*
(   - "She earned a Bachelor of Science in Biotechnology.") Tj
T*
(   - "He holds a Master of Science degree.") Tj
T*
(   - "She was awarded a PhD in Molecular Genetics.") Tj
T*
(   - Specific Thesis / Dissertation \(Takes Definite Article\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The PhD thesis submitted by Dr. Roy elucidated telomeric heterochromatin.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Fellowship and Honors:) Tj
T*
(   - "He was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society.") Tj
T*
(   - "She received the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine in 2020." \(Nobel Prize takes 'the'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 26:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze article usage before words like 'Nature', 'Society', 'Space', and 'Earth' in scientific writing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Specialized Abstract Words Taking Zero Article:) Tj
T*
(   - Nature \(The physical universe / ecosystem\):) Tj
T*
(   - Takes ZERO article when referring to the natural world:) Tj
T*
(   - "Such spontaneous mutations occur frequently in nature." \(Never *in the nature\).) Tj
T*
(   - Contrast: "The nature of the chemical bond" \(Restricted by 'of'-phrase -> takes 'the'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Society \(Human civilization collectively\):) Tj
T*
(   - "Biotechnology offers immense benefits to society." \(Not *to the society\).) Tj
T*
(   - Space \(The physical cosmos\):) Tj
T*
(   - "Radiation exposure in space presents biological hazards." \(Not *in the space\).) Tj
T*
(   - Contrast: "The space between the two electrodes" \(Takes 'the'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Celestial Bodies:) Tj
T*
(   - Earth: Typically takes the definite article: "Life evolved on the Earth" or "on Earth" \(both) Tj
T*
(   acceptable, 'the Earth' is more formal\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 27:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss determiner placement before coordinate adjectives and noun compounds in assay descriptions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Scope of Determiners Across Coordinate Adjectives:) Tj
T*
(   When a single determiner precedes multiple coordinate adjectives modifying a singular noun, its) Tj
T*
(   semantic scope extends over all adjectives:) Tj
T*
(   - "a rapid, sensitive, and reproducible assay") Tj
T*
(   - Analysis: 'A' applies to the unified composite concept of the assay. Repeating the article) Tj
T*
(   \(*a rapid, a sensitive, and a reproducible assay\) is redundant and ungrammatical when) Tj
T*
(   describing a single test.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Compound Noun Distinctions:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
